WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.384
After his kingdom fell, Li Yu was taken north, and could return to the south only in his dreams.

00:00:06.734 --> 00:00:12.254
Spring flowers and autumn moon — gazing at the bright moon in the sky, he thought of the palaces of his lost kingdom.

00:00:12.604 --> 00:00:18.436
He picked up his brush and wrote 'Yu Meiren'; every single word was longing.

00:00:18.786 --> 00:00:24.618
Outside the window the spring wind blew past, and his tears quietly fell.

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:33.152
The carved railings and jade steps are still there today; only the rosy faces have changed — the past is too painful to look back on.

00:00:33.502 --> 00:00:38.182
Gazing toward the south, he thought of the days gone by.

00:00:38.532 --> 00:00:44.964
Ask me how much sorrow I can bear — it is just like a river of spring water flowing east.

00:00:45.314 --> 00:00:51.098
The river water flowed east without stopping, just like his sorrow, which had no end.

00:00:51.448 --> 00:00:57.400
This poem has been passed down for a thousand years, and Li Yu became the most famous poet of a fallen kingdom.

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:03.174
People reading this poem can all feel his deep sorrow.

